    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4880" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ballistārĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">balist-</span></b> ; and in Gloss. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ballistrārĭus</span></b> ),
			ii, m.
		1. ballista. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A maker of ballistœ</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 50, 6,
				6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">COLLEGIVM BALLISTARIORVM.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4066</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>One who discharges the ballista</i>, <i>a slinger</i>, <i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 2,
				2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 16, 2, 5</span></i>.</div>
